{"name":"Asian Fusion","hex":"#ece0cd","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fusion","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of merging separate things, or the result thereof.\n\n A nuclear reaction in which nuclei combine to form more massive nuclei with the concomitant release of energy. \n A style of music that blends disparate genres; especially different types of jazz and reggae.\nA style of cooking that combines ingredients and techniques from different countries or cultures\nThe act of melting or liquefying something by heating it.\n\n The result of the hybridation of two genes which originally coded for separate proteins.\n The process by which two distinct lipid bilayers merge their hydrophobic core, resulting in one interconnected structure.\n The act of two characters merging into one, typically more powerful, being; or the merged being itself.","A nuclear reaction in which nuclei combine to form more massive nuclei with the concomitant release of energy."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To combine; to fuse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fusion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fusion cuisine","blocks":[{"text":"Fusion cuisine is a cuisine that combines elements of different culinary traditions that originate from different countries, regions, or cultures. Cuisines of this type are not categorized according to any one particular cuisine style and have played a part in many contemporary restaurant cuisines since the 1970s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/Minchi_e_bacalhaus.jpg/330px-Minchi_e_bacalhaus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fusion_cuisine","wikidata":"Q601763"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Gobi_manchurian.jpg/500px-Gobi_manchurian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Gobi_manchurian.jpg/500px-Gobi_manchurian.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gobi Manchurian is an Indian–Chinese fusion dish, consisting of fried cauliflower. The dish is popular throughout India and Indian restaurants as well as South Asian restaurants around the world.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGobi_manchurian.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Red_roast_duck_curry.jpg/500px-Red_roast_duck_curry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Red_roast_duck_curry.jpg/1280px-Red_roast_duck_curry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Red_roast_duck_curry.jpg/500px-Red_roast_duck_curry.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kaeng phet pet yang (Thai roast duck curry) is an example of early fusion cuisine of the cosmopolitan court of the Ayutthaya Kingdom, combining Thai red curry, Chinese roast duck, and grapes originally from Persia.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_roast_duck_curry.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/03368jfNagwaling_Diwa_National_Roads_Welcome_Pilar_Bataanfvf_26.JPG/500px-03368jfNagwaling_Diwa_National_Roads_Welcome_Pilar_Bataanfvf_26.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/03368jfNagwaling_Diwa_National_Roads_Welcome_Pilar_Bataanfvf_26.JPG/1280px-03368jfNagwaling_Diwa_National_Roads_Welcome_Pilar_Bataanfvf_26.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/66/03368jfNagwaling_Diwa_National_Roads_Welcome_Pilar_Bataanfvf_26.JPG/500px-03368jfNagwali